Do you make effective use of your pet(s)?

The point is that wizards and healers need to gain levels much slower
than they descend through the dungeon. (Especially gnomish healers; the
reward for the protection racket is actually worth the effort and risk
in that case.)  Combat characters can afford to gain levels; their
weaponry and stats give them the power to survive (although I've lost
valks to soldier ants an annoying number of times.)

Your pet will kill monsters for you; the more monsters it kills, the
better it gets at killing monsters.  A 9th-level pet can deal with most
9HD or less monsters (except perhaps military types and mumakil).
Soldier ants are flimsy (3HD, so 13hp on average), but they're quick and
hard to hit and quite hard-hitting.

